<task id="034" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Self-service submitter authz (Tier-2 requester==caller) + app-only SPE upload</title>
    <phase>P3 Legal Front Door intake MVP</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:030,031</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Security-sensitive: authorization predicate + app-only SPE broker upload; tags include auth + bff-api; modifies .cs on the shared external-access surface — FULL per CLAUDE.md §8 (auth tag, security-sensitive).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security + shared-surface: Tier-2 authorization predicate (NFR-08) + app-only SPE broker path (ADR-007, no OBO) with a hard escalation boundary; high blast radius on the external-access surface shared with teams-app-r1.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Auth + SPE on the shared external-access BFF surface; must serialize with other BFF external-access work; 035 depends on this authz.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>030,031</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Enforce the Legal Front Door Tier-2 record-scope predicate — requester == caller (a submitter sees/acts on ONLY their own requests, NFR-08) — server-side on the Front Door endpoint group, and implement document upload as an app-only SPE stream via the SpeFileStore broker (ADR-007): no OBO, no Graph-pointer exposure, keyed on documentId, with authorization-before-stream (403 → zero bytes, no Graph call). Also implement lazy Contact attribution (bind workforce oid → requester Contact) on first submission (FR-11).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Security-sensitive: server-enforced authorization, app-only broker patterns, SPE integration. No client-trusted authz.</role>
  <goal>The Front Door group enforces requester==caller for every read/get/upload (user A cannot see or touch user B's requests or documents); document upload streams app-only through SpeFileStore keyed on documentId with authz-before-stream; an internal user's first submission lazily resolves-or-creates their Contact by oid and sets it as requester. All decisions are server-side; negative cases return ProblemDetails 403 with no bytes and no Graph call.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-17: A Front Door user (workforce SSO) can create and see only their own requests (Tier-2 predicate requester==caller, one instance of NFR-08's per-module record-scope); document upload streams app-only via the SPE broker (no OBO, no pointer exposure). FR-11: on an internal user's first attributed action, resolve-or-create a Contact by workforce oid (reuse R1 ResolveOrCreateContact + bind-oid to sprk_externalobjectid) and record as requester; no Contact created merely by having access. NFR-01: external CIAM broker-only; workforce SPA path no-OBO. NFR-06/08: server-enforced; negative Tier-2 test required per module. teams-app-r1 shipped CallerPrincipalResolver + CallerPrincipal (GetAccessibleProjectIds/GetAccessLevel) and IAccessibleRecordSetService as the canonical NFR-08 worked example — Front Door's predicate is the simpler requester==caller variant on the resolved CallerPrincipal. ADR-007: SpeFileStore facade for all SPE ops.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs (CallerPrincipal :66, resolver — the resolved caller identity to compare against requester)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter.cs:29 (group-level filter setting CallerPrincipal on HttpContext.Items)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/** — the 031 MapFrontDoorEndpoints group (add the requester==caller predicate + upload here)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/InviteExternalUserEndpoint.cs (ResolveOrCreateContactAsync :172; oid → sprk_externalobjectid :139 — reuse for lazy attribution)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs (resolve-by-oid :231 / bind-oid :323 — reuse)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-007-spefilestore.md + .claude/skills/spe-integration/SKILL.md (SpeFileStore app-only upload; authz-before-stream)</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (binding BFF governance)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>030 (sprk_servicerequest.requester + submitted-document linkage) and 031 (Front Door endpoint group) must be complete. 035 (my-requests UI) depends on this server-side authz.</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">The Front Door Tier-2 predicate MUST be requester==caller enforced SERVER-side on every read/get/list/upload in the group — module entitlement (Tier 1) MUST NOT grant visibility to another user's requests. A negative test (user A cannot access user B's request/document) is REQUIRED.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">All document upload MUST go through the SpeFileStore facade as an APP-ONLY stream — no OBO, no direct Graph client in the endpoint, no SPE pointer/driveItem URL returned to the SPA; endpoints key on documentId only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Authorization-before-stream: the requester==caller (and document ownership) check MUST run BEFORE any Graph/SPE call — an unauthorized upload/download returns ProblemDetails 403 with ZERO bytes streamed and NO Graph call made (verified by test).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01">The CIAM path stays broker-only and the workforce SPA path stays no-OBO — do NOT introduce token exchange or OBO to satisfy the app-only upload. (See escalation.)</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-11">Lazy Contact attribution MUST reuse R1 ResolveOrCreateContactAsync + bind-oid to sprk_externalobjectid; create/link exactly ONE Contact on first submission; subsequent submissions reuse it; NO Contact is created merely by having module access.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF addition: state Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); dotnet publish -c Release, report compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB baseline (≤60 MB); no new HIGH CVE; /conflict-check before the BFF PR (teams-app-r1 shares this surface).</constraint>
  </constraints>
