    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Plane-agnostic caller" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs">Resolve CallerPrincipal from the group filter; Front Door predicate compares requester == resolved caller (oid/ContactId).</pattern>
      <pattern name="Lazy Contact by oid" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/InviteExternalUserEndpoint.cs">Reuse ResolveOrCreateContactAsync :172 + oid → sprk_externalobjectid :139.</pattern>
      <pattern name="App-only SPE" location=".claude/skills/spe-integration/SKILL.md">SpeFileStore facade, app-only, documentId-keyed; authz before stream; never return Graph pointers.</pattern>
      <pattern name="NFR-08 predicate" location="spec.md NFR-08">teams-app-r1 IAccessibleRecordSetService is the participation-grant variant; Front Door is the simpler submitter-owned (requester==caller) variant.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load FR-11/FR-17, NFR-01/06/08, ADR-007/028, spe-integration skill, and the 031 Front Door group. Run /conflict-check for the external-access surface.</step>
    <step order="2">Confirm the app-only SPE upload path is achievable through SpeFileStore without OBO. If it is NOT (e.g., app-only broker cannot satisfy the upload without an OBO token), STOP and escalate per &lt;escalation&gt; — do NOT introduce OBO.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement lazy Contact attribution on submit: resolve-or-create the caller's Contact by workforce oid (reuse ResolveOrCreateContactAsync + bind-oid), set as sprk_servicerequest.requester; ensure exactly one Contact per user and none created without a submission.</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the requester==caller Tier-2 predicate: gate every Front Door read/get/list so a caller only sees requests where requester == resolved CallerPrincipal; deny others with ProblemDetails 403 (server-side, not client-filtered).</step>
    <step order="5">Implement document upload: authz-before-stream (verify requester==caller + document ownership), then stream app-only through SpeFileStore keyed on documentId; never return a Graph pointer/driveItem URL. Persist the submitted-document linkage (030 schema).</step>
    <step order="6">Tests (ADR-038 KEEP-path, tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/): (a) user A cannot GET/list user B's request → 403; (b) unauthorized upload → 403 with zero bytes AND no Graph call (assert the SPE/Graph client was not invoked); (c) first submission creates exactly one Contact bound by oid; second reuses it; (d) no Contact created by access alone. NO Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; / DI-registration / ctor-null tests.</step>
    <step order="7">Build: dotnet publish -c Release; report compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB (≤60 MB); dotnet list package --vulnerable (no new HIGH). State Placement Justification in notes/PR.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviations in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the app-only SPE upload path CANNOT be satisfied through the SpeFileStore broker without introducing OBO or a downstream token exchange, STOP and escalate via 🔔 Human Input Required (CLAUDE.md §6 + NFR-01): app-only broker-only is a hard security invariant. Do NOT silently add OBO to make the upload work — present the blocker + options and wait for owner direction.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell, /conflict-check, dotnet list package --vulnerable</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Not required (server task; client upload UX is 031/035)</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/** — requester==caller Tier-2 predicate on the Front Door group + app-only SpeFileStore upload (documentId-keyed) + lazy Contact attribution</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/** — two-user isolation (403), unauthorized-upload (403/no-bytes/no-Graph), one-Contact-on-first-submission, no-Contact-by-access-alone</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given user A's request, when user B (entitled to the Front Door module) GETs/lists it, then the server returns ProblemDetails 403 and B never receives A's data — enforced server-side, not client-filtered (negative Tier-2 test, NFR-08).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an unauthorized upload attempt, when it hits the upload endpoint, then authz runs before any stream → ProblemDetails 403 with ZERO bytes streamed and NO Graph/SPE call made (asserted in test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an authorized submitter, when they upload a document, then it streams app-only through SpeFileStore keyed on documentId; the response returns NO Graph pointer/driveItem URL (NFR-01, MUST-NOT expose Graph pointers).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an internal user's first submission, when it is processed, then exactly one Contact is resolved-or-created by workforce oid (bound to sprk_externalobjectid) and set as requester; a second submission reuses it (FR-11).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: merely having Front Door module entitlement (Tier 1) creates NO Contact and grants NO visibility to other users' requests (Tier 1 ≠ Tier 2).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the BFF build, when dotnet publish -c Release runs, then compressed size is reported with delta vs 46.90 MB, is ≤60 MB, and dotnet list package --vulnerable shows no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>Spec FR-11/FR-17, NFR-01/06/08, ADR-007/028/034. teams-app-r1 IAccessibleRecordSetService is the participation variant of NFR-08; Front Door is the simpler requester==caller variant on the resolved CallerPrincipal — reuse the resolver + filter, do NOT rebuild. Reuse ResolveOrCreateContactAsync + bind-oid for lazy attribution. Hard invariant: app-only, no OBO, no Graph pointers, authz-before-stream — escalate rather than violate. §10 BFF: Placement Justification + publish delta + CVE + /conflict-check mandatory.</notes>
